.TH DISCIPLINE 1 "2026-08-18" "realisateur" "bashified verb"
.SH NAME
discipline \- print the realisateur baseline: build-discipline checklist and ecosystem protocols
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B discipline
.br
.B discipline
--checklist
.br
.B discipline
--protocols
.br
.B discipline
--path
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the baseline every project in this ecosystem is held to: what to check
before calling work done, and what to do when a change reaches outside the
repository you are in.
.PP
The text has exactly one home,
.BR BUILD-DISCIPLINE.md ,
and is read at the point of use rather than copied. Stamping it into
seventeen repositories is what produced eleven byte-identical corrupted
copies and a source thirty-six lines behind its own copies, with a drift
detector reporting OK throughout.
.PP
Run it before marking anything done. If it is not on PATH, that is a
finding: say so. Do not recite the checklist from memory and do not perform
its steps by hand. A missing guard is a finding, not an inconvenience.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --checklist
Print only the build-discipline checklist.
.TP
.B --protocols
Print only the ecosystem protocols \(em the cross-repository half.
.TP
.B --path
Print the file the text was read from. Use this to prove which copy you got.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The baseline was printed.
.TP
.B 1
The source text could not be found or contains no fenced baseline block.
.SH NOTES
Installed host-wide as a symlink into the verb build, so the file resolves
its own location with
.BR "readlink -f" .
Without that, the parent directory reads as
.I /usr/local
and the text is never found.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR closeout-lint (1),
.BR silence-audit (1),
.BR notify-senechal (1)
